{# Start the timeline request while the component bundle is still downloading.

   <release-timeline> fetches what it draws from the JSON API when it mounts,
   which is *after* the bundle has arrived and parsed. The request and the
   bundle therefore happen one after the other rather than at the same time,
   and the gutter sits empty for a round trip longer than it has to.

   This starts the same request during HTML parse and parks the promise where
   the component picks it up, keyed by URL — see fetchTimeline in
   frontend/src/lib/api.js, which consumes it once and then goes to the network
   like normal, so live refreshes are never served a page-load payload.

   It never rejects: a failure resolves to null and the component falls back to
   fetching normally, so there is still one place that decides what a failed
   timeline looks like.

   Deliberately *not* the payload inlined into the page. That would remove the
   request altogether, but it puts the whole timeline back on the server's
   critical path for every page load — the work deleted in #264 — and on the
   org-wide page that meant one request per project before the HTML could be
   sent. This costs the server nothing.

   The URL travels as a data attribute rather than interpolated into the script
   body: these templates render with autoescaping off, and an attribute has one
   escaping rule (`|escape`) rather than JavaScript's several. #}
{% macro timeline_prefetch(org, project) %}
{% set url = ("/api/orgs/" ~ org ~ "/projects/" ~ project ~ "/timeline") if project else ("/api/orgs/" ~ org ~ "/timeline") %}
<script data-timeline-url="{{ url|escape }}">
(function () {
    var el = document.currentScript;
    if (!el) return;
    var url = el.getAttribute("data-timeline-url");
    var store = (window.__forestTimeline = window.__forestTimeline || {});
    store[url] = fetch(url, { credentials: "same-origin" })
        .then(function (r) { return r.ok ? r.json() : null; })
        .catch(function () { return null; });
})();
</script>
{% endmacro %}
